[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n4_hugh"
text = "# DRAFT
# Prior Hugh at dusk, on the north walk (night 4, fog). Cold; he's investigating. He heard two men run the cloister
# after Matins last night and wants to know what the porter saw. If the porter has told him the truth before
# (n3_told_prior, or everything at night 2's dawn), he says so. Telling him about the crypt: Suspicion +10 (Ranulf overhears).
# If the keys were copied (keys_copied), he looks at them and finds the wax: where were they? (n4_hugh_keys)
== start
(The prior comes out of the fog so close you nearly walk into him. His wax tablet is already open.)
Hugh: Porter. Two men ran the cloister last night after Matins, one behind the other. I heard them from this walk.
Hugh: The first of them was you.
-> before [if n3_told_prior]
-> before [if n2_told_hugh=thomas]
-> ask

== before
Hugh: You've told me the truth before, and I wrote it down. Do it again.
-> ask

== ask
Hugh: What did you see?
* [if died_crypt_pilgrim] I saw a bound man killed at the altar in the crypt. -> crypt
* It was the demon, Father Prior. -> demon
* It wasn't me, Father Prior. I was never there. -> denied

# Telling the prior anything: Suspicion +10, because Ranulf overhears (design doc).
== crypt [set n4_hugh_night=crypt] [suspicion 10]
(You tell him: the light, the bound man, the figure at the altar. He writes it all on the wax.)
(Somewhere in the fog behind you, a door closes softly.)
Hugh: Under the saint's altar. Tell no one else. Not the abbot. Not anyone.
-> keys [if keys_copied]
-> end

== demon [set n4_hugh_night=demon]
Hugh: The demon. The abbot's word for it.
Hugh: Whatever ran behind you was out of breath, porter. I heard it. Demons don't pant.
-> keys [if keys_copied]
-> end

== denied [set n4_hugh_night=denied] [trust hugh -5]
Hugh: Then someone wears your face. I'll find out who.
-> keys [if keys_copied]
-> end

== keys [note keys_moved]
Hugh: Your keys. Give them here.
(He turns them in the grey light and scrapes a tooth with his thumbnail. Wax comes away.)
Hugh: Someone has taken a mould of these. When were they out of your hands?
* [if n3_thomas_hid_you] I was in the infirmary last night, with Brother Thomas. -> keys_thomas
* I don't know, Father Prior. -> keys_unknown
* They've never left me, Father Prior. -> keys_lie

== keys_thomas [set n4_hugh_keys=thomas]
Hugh: With Thomas. All night, and your keys on your belt the whole while.
(He writes one word on the wax, and gives the keys back.)
Hugh: A lock two men have a key to is no lock, porter. Remember that tonight.
-> end

== keys_unknown [set n4_hugh_keys=unknown]
Hugh: You don't know. The porter, and he doesn't know where his keys go at night.
Hugh: A lock two men have a key to is no lock. Remember that tonight.
-> end

== keys_lie [set n4_hugh_keys=lie] [trust hugh -5]
Hugh: Then the wax grew on them by itself. (He drops them in your hand.)
Hugh: A lock two men have a key to is no lock, porter. Remember that tonight.
-> end

== again
(The prior is a dark shape in the fog, writing.)
Hugh: Go, porter. And keep your keys on you.
-> end

== leave
Hugh: I'll find you, porter. In fog or out of it.
"
